<!-- Onboarding window (resources/lib/onboarding_app.py): what the TV shows while the phone works through a flow with
     steps, here the Google key wizard. A dim backdrop and one rounded card: the steps on the left, the rows of chips
     ("on the Google page tap ..."), a warning and the status badges on the right, a footer with the key hints.
     Window properties: kicker, title1, title2 (the title cut into its two lines), header ("Step 2 of 4 . ..."), warn,
     footer, and for the chips chip1..12 (the label, with colour markup), chip1_bg..chip12_bg (the fill), sep1..12 and
     then1..3 (the words between them; "" for a slot not in use).
     Controls: 20 the list of steps (items: t1, t2 (the second line, "" for a step that fits one), state done | now | todo,
     num, fg (colour of the words and number), ring (colour of the ring)), 30 the list of badges (items: t1, bg, fg).
     101..112 chip pictures and 201..212 chip labels, 301..312 separators, 401..403 "Then": all of them start at the
     corner of the chip area, and Python moves and widens them (the widths follow the words, onboarding_view.layout_chips);
     50 the warning, which Python puts under the last row of chips.
     Nothing here takes the focus or is animated; the lists never show a cursor (the focused layout is the plain one).
     Budget (Pi 3B+): backdrop, shadow, card, divider, at most 8 step markers, 12 chips and 6 badges: 30 pictures. -->
